{
  "question_id": "q_038_rolling_average_tweets",
  "slug": "rolling-average-tweets",
  "title": "Tweets' Rolling Averages",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "company": "Twitter",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "Given a table of tweet data over a specified time period, calculate the 3-day rolling average of tweets for each user. Output the user ID, tweet date, and rolling averages rounded to 2 decimal places.\n\nNotes:\n\n*Effective April 7th, 2023, the problem statement, solution and hints for this question have been revised.*",
  "notes": [
    "A rolling average, also known as a moving average or running mean is a time-series technique that examines trends in data over a specified period of time.",
    "In this case, we want to determine how the tweet count for each user changes over a 3-day period.",
    "The dataset you are querying against may have different input & output - this is just an example!"
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "tweets",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "user_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "tweet_date",
          "data_type": "DATETIME"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "tweet_count",
          "data_type": "INT"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "tweets": [
      {
        "user_id": "111",
        "tweet_date": "06/01/2022 00:00:00",
        "tweet_count": "2"
      },
      {
        "user_id": "111",
